WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.063 --> 00:01.054
(All characters, locations, and events are fictional

3
00:01.079 --> 00:02.031
and for entertainment purposes only.

4
00:02.055 --> 00:03.070
No actions depicted are intended to be encouraged or endorsed.

5
00:03.095 --> 00:04.189
Animals were specially trained and supervised by professionals.

6
00:04.214 --> 00:05.570
Viewer discretion is advised.)

7
00:07.034 --> 00:09.531
A lot of people say golf is all about competition.

8
00:10.523 --> 00:13.167
But to me, it's really a test of heart.

9
00:14.882 --> 00:17.856
Some holes feel too long. Sometimes the wind is too strong.

10
00:19.627 --> 00:22.893
But if you never swing, you've already lost before you begin.

11
00:24.273 --> 00:26.157
Love is probably no different.

12
00:26.659 --> 00:28.662
Even if you don't know whether it'll find the hole,

13
00:28.687 --> 00:31.092
you still have to be brave enough to take the first shot.

14
00:32.442 --> 00:34.087
Whatever the outcome,

15
00:34.111 --> 00:36.111
all you can do is accept it.

16
00:42.229 --> 00:44.476
(Pro Sherry: Tiranan Yoopan)

17
00:54.885 --> 00:58.297
♪ Everyone can tell by the way you stare ♪

18
00:59.022 --> 01:00.746
♪ Sneaking little looks when I'm unaware ♪

19
01:00.771 --> 01:04.225
♪ It's plain to see ♪

20
01:04.886 --> 01:06.545
♪ I know exactly what you think of me ♪

21
01:06.570 --> 01:09.970
♪ First to watch my stories every time ♪

22
01:10.654 --> 01:12.369
♪ You remember every fave of mine ♪

23
01:12.394 --> 01:15.934
♪ Everywhere I go, you're by my side ♪

24
01:16.351 --> 01:18.153
♪ Don't tell me there's nothing on your mind ♪

25
01:18.178 --> 01:21.107
♪ So when are you gonna say the words? ♪

26
01:21.132 --> 01:22.991
♪ Don't keep me waiting till it hurts ♪

27
01:23.016 --> 01:25.804
♪ The way you act, I know you're into me ♪

28
01:25.829 --> 01:28.712
♪ That racing heart gives you away so easily ♪

29
01:28.737 --> 01:32.555
♪ But I'll play clueless, just wait and see ♪

30
01:32.580 --> 01:34.580
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

31
01:34.605 --> 01:37.426
♪ Giving me signs, so why still wait? ♪

32
01:37.451 --> 01:40.930
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

33
01:40.955 --> 01:45.640
♪ How long will you keep playing so tough? ♪

34
01:45.665 --> 01:47.665
♪ Or should I be the one to call your bluff? ♪

35
01:49.072 --> 01:51.996
Stay calm. Focus on the shot in front of you.

36
01:54.593 --> 01:56.772
Six strokes on a par five.

37
01:56.797 --> 01:59.386
Two better than the limit I gave you. You did it.

38
01:59.411 --> 02:02.515
Yes! I did it! I actually did it!

39
02:02.540 --> 02:05.733
See? When you really commit, nothing is impossible.

40
02:05.758 --> 02:09.865
Your swing is steadier, and your timing is much better. Good job.

41
02:09.890 --> 02:11.760
Who have you been learning from?

42
02:11.785 --> 02:13.783
Pro Jin at The Royal Green.

43
02:13.808 --> 02:16.689
You can't invite her here. Those two don't get along.

44
02:16.968 --> 02:18.262
Who doesn't?

45
02:18.287 --> 02:21.151
Pro Vee and Pro Jin.

46
02:21.176 --> 02:24.150
I heard Nana took a lesson from you.

47
02:24.175 --> 02:27.256
You're good. You figured out your student pretty quickly.

48
02:27.281 --> 02:28.803
Too bad I couldn't read my own friend

49
02:28.828 --> 02:31.339
before she betrayed me, even after knowing her for so long.

50
02:31.364 --> 02:32.632
Miss Nana, we've got a problem.

51
02:32.657 --> 02:34.213
The tour group that booked our course

52
02:34.238 --> 02:35.746
just canceled the entire reservation.

53
02:39.863 --> 02:44.931
Everyone, we're not here today for me to tell you what to do.

54
02:45.111 --> 02:46.680
We're here to figure it out together.

55
02:46.705 --> 02:50.030
How do we make Goodview number one again, like it used to be?

56
02:50.055 --> 02:51.719
We're not doing this just for the course.

57
02:51.744 --> 02:53.154
We're doing it for ourselves.

58
02:53.178 --> 02:55.113
Because if the course becomes profitable again,

59
02:55.138 --> 02:58.357
all of us benefit from the rewards that come with it.

60
02:58.590 --> 03:03.371
Our goal is to make this a place everyone wants to come to,

61
03:03.396 --> 03:05.303
golfers and non-golfers alike.

62
03:05.328 --> 03:08.983
So no idea is too wild or too unconventional.

63
03:09.008 --> 03:10.403
Our first response will always be,

64
03:10.428 --> 03:11.744
"That's a good idea."

65
03:12.188 --> 03:13.984
Then we'll build on it together.

66
03:14.009 --> 03:15.920
No shooting ideas down. No arguing against them.

67
03:15.945 --> 03:18.518
Each group gets one hour.

68
03:18.543 --> 03:19.637
Go ahead.

69
03:41.761 --> 03:43.664
Every idea we hear...

70
03:43.689 --> 03:46.244
- is a good idea. - is a good idea.

71
03:46.571 --> 03:48.439
Our group's idea is "Date on the Green."

72
03:48.638 --> 03:50.090
This one's from my team.

73
03:50.115 --> 03:51.604
That's a good idea.

74
03:51.629 --> 03:54.302
We'd offer date packages for couples at the course.

75
03:54.327 --> 03:57.183
A lot of couples are looking for new places to go on dates.

76
03:57.208 --> 03:59.920
We already have meal sets and photographers ready to go.

77
03:59.945 --> 04:01.404
I like it. Sold.

78
04:02.502 --> 04:04.232
And by late afternoon or evening,

79
04:04.257 --> 04:06.115
most golfers are already done for the day.

80
04:06.139 --> 04:08.004
It's better than leaving the course empty.

81
04:08.029 --> 04:09.556
I think it's a great idea.

82
04:09.698 --> 04:12.035
Thank you.

83
04:12.942 --> 04:14.465
As for this team...

84
04:15.095 --> 04:17.063
"Caddie in Character."

85
04:17.088 --> 04:20.825
We'd divide our caddies into four different styles

86
04:20.850 --> 04:22.832
for different types of golfers.

87
04:22.857 --> 04:25.064
- Exactly. - Nice.

88
04:25.247 --> 04:27.104
Based on customer feedback,

89
04:27.129 --> 04:29.207
people want caddies who can read the room.

90
04:29.274 --> 04:31.854
Some days, golfers want a quiet round,

91
04:31.879 --> 04:33.538
but the caddie keeps chatting.

92
04:33.569 --> 04:36.479
Sometimes they want advice on a particular shot,

93
04:36.504 --> 04:38.645
but the caddie doesn't know the course well enough.

94
04:38.670 --> 04:41.421
And sometimes the caddie should help set the mood,

95
04:41.446 --> 04:43.184
because some major business deals

96
04:43.209 --> 04:44.712
get closed right here on the course.

97
04:44.736 --> 04:48.960
Hmm... And if the clients are happy,

98
04:48.985 --> 04:51.209
the caddies might even get bigger tips.

99
04:52.298 --> 04:53.314
Good.

100
04:54.273 --> 04:56.499
As for Pro Jin's Golf Academy,

101
04:57.134 --> 04:58.586
that's a no-brainer.

102
04:59.250 --> 05:01.673
We'll also have tailored programs

103
05:01.698 --> 05:05.786
for kids, teens, women, and business professionals.

104
05:05.811 --> 05:07.463
Let's move forward with it.

105
05:07.709 --> 05:10.070
I'd like to add a program for seniors too.

106
05:10.570 --> 05:13.244
They're another group we should be focusing on.

107
05:13.530 --> 05:15.504
Good. That's a good idea.

108
05:16.856 --> 05:20.422
And from my darling August's team, we have Golf E-Sports.

109
05:21.207 --> 05:23.919
We'll recreate our course in an online golf game.

110
05:24.126 --> 05:27.799
Then I've got E-Food. That's my idea.

111
05:27.824 --> 05:31.242
We photograph our dishes and put the menu online.

112
05:31.267 --> 05:34.729
People coming to the course can order their food in advance.

113
05:34.754 --> 05:39.147
And even if they're not coming, they can still order delivery.

114
05:39.273 --> 05:41.167
- Can our team handle that? - Absolutely.

115
05:41.192 --> 05:43.937
- There you go. - Good. That's a great idea.

116
05:46.058 --> 05:48.912
As for Pro Vee's group, I'm not quite following yet.

117
05:48.937 --> 05:51.216
Could you explain it a little more?

118
05:51.389 --> 05:54.898
It's not really a new idea. A lot of courses already do it.

119
05:54.923 --> 05:56.907
We used to do it here too.

120
05:56.946 --> 06:00.356
But I think bringing it back could add some excitement.

121
06:00.381 --> 06:02.745
Great. That's a good idea. Approved.

122
06:02.770 --> 06:04.376
She hasn't even told you the idea yet.

123
06:04.401 --> 06:07.163
Oh. Right. Go ahead.

124
06:07.311 --> 06:08.404
A Pro-Am.

125
06:09.254 --> 06:11.716
Pro Am? We have a pro named Am here?

126
06:11.741 --> 06:13.773
I thought we only had Pro Vee, Pro Jin, and Pro...

127
06:13.798 --> 06:17.991
No, no. A Pro-Am is an event where amateur golfers

128
06:18.016 --> 06:20.637
get paired up with professional golfers.

129
06:20.662 --> 06:24.109
They could be pros from our course or guest pros we invite.

130
06:24.547 --> 06:26.110
Normally, at these events,

131
06:26.135 --> 06:31.097
they invite sponsors, major partners, and the media.

132
06:31.122 --> 06:35.539
But ours would also give regular golfers at our course

133
06:35.564 --> 06:37.333
the chance to play a round with a pro.

134
06:37.829 --> 06:40.108
We could charge an additional fee

135
06:40.133 --> 06:42.910
and hold it on special occasions.

136
06:46.338 --> 06:49.426
But won't all the pretty pros get hit on?

137
06:50.888 --> 06:53.217
Hmm? Jealous?

138
06:53.955 --> 06:56.331
- Concerned. - Sure.

139
07:03.804 --> 07:05.882
I've got an idea too.

140
07:06.350 --> 07:08.755
I'd like to propose a Night Golf project.

141
07:09.149 --> 07:11.388
But it won't just be playing under the lights at night.

142
07:11.413 --> 07:14.977
We'll also have handsome male caddies looking after our guests.

143
07:20.506 --> 07:23.885
Before anyone gets the wrong idea, let me explain.

144
07:24.528 --> 07:28.166
I don't want us to assume that having men serve women

145
07:28.191 --> 07:30.064
or women serve men

146
07:30.089 --> 07:32.656
always has to be sexual.

147
07:32.681 --> 07:35.849
Sometimes it's simply another form of entertainment

148
07:35.874 --> 07:38.440
that makes people feel confident and brings positive energy.

149
07:38.465 --> 07:40.879
We're not selling sex. We're not selling looks.

150
07:40.904 --> 07:44.787
We're selling atmosphere, fun, and the feeling of being special.

151
07:45.097 --> 07:49.710
Golf courses have traditionally been seen as a man's space.

152
07:49.735 --> 07:53.263
I want women to feel that this place belongs to them too.

153
07:53.288 --> 07:55.402
Not by diminishing men,

154
07:55.427 --> 07:57.214
but by bringing in something fresh.

155
07:57.239 --> 07:58.795
If I may add something,

156
07:58.820 --> 08:01.013
the female golf market is growing every year.

157
08:01.038 --> 08:03.276
Nightlife experiences are also becoming more popular,

158
08:03.301 --> 08:05.396
and younger customers are looking for activities

159
08:05.421 --> 08:07.503
worth photographing and sharing.

160
08:07.527 --> 08:09.229
I think it's a great idea.

161
08:09.254 --> 08:12.184
We can position golf as entertainment, as something fun,

162
08:12.209 --> 08:14.637
and create a new image for golf.

163
08:14.662 --> 08:16.821
Instead of going out to a pub or bar,

164
08:16.846 --> 08:18.727
why not come to a golf course?

165
08:18.752 --> 08:20.825
I'll summarize all of today's ideas

166
08:20.850 --> 08:24.512
and put together a proposal for the management team.

167
08:24.774 --> 08:26.774
Including the budget and timeline.

168
08:26.970 --> 08:28.168
Thanks, Belle.

169
08:29.996 --> 08:32.869
And thank you, everyone, for sharing your ideas today.

170
08:33.067 --> 08:36.430
Goodview is going to be one of the top golf courses again.

171
08:37.042 --> 08:38.360
Allez, allez!

172
08:38.385 --> 08:41.289
- Huh? - What does that mean?

173
08:42.011 --> 08:45.575
"Allez, allez" is French for "Come on, everyone! Let's go!"

174
08:45.734 --> 08:49.244
All right, everyone. We've got a new one. One, two, three...

175
08:49.420 --> 08:52.120
Allez, allez!

176
09:44.900 --> 09:46.729
The breaker looks fine.

177
09:47.332 --> 09:50.062
Why is your power out? Mine's still on.

178
09:50.558 --> 09:52.068
Do you know how to fix it?

179
09:55.061 --> 09:56.594
I'm not an electrician.

180
09:57.498 --> 09:59.424
Shouldn't you call one?

181
10:00.320 --> 10:02.035
It's really late.

182
10:02.430 --> 10:04.399
I'd feel bad calling them out now.

183
10:04.424 --> 10:05.819
But you don't feel bad calling me?

184
10:08.491 --> 10:10.079
Wait, wait.

185
10:11.774 --> 10:15.567
You said the power at your place is still on, right?

186
10:22.177 --> 10:24.934
Then can I stay over tonight?

187
10:29.378 --> 10:30.783
Make yourself at home, Pro Vee.

188
10:31.045 --> 10:33.045
Shouldn't I be the one saying that?

189
10:52.803 --> 10:54.062
I'm turning the light off.

190
10:57.762 --> 10:59.432
Chomp, chomp.

191
11:02.218 --> 11:03.396
What are you doing?

192
11:03.658 --> 11:05.606
You never played this when you were little?

193
11:05.836 --> 11:07.836
Chomp, chomp.

194
11:08.298 --> 11:09.872
You're such a kid.

195
11:10.089 --> 11:12.374
Oh, so you've never done it.

196
11:13.242 --> 11:16.075
Or maybe... you just don't know how.

197
11:21.003 --> 11:23.751
Wow. Did you really have to show off?

198
11:24.748 --> 11:27.017
Fine. Then try this.

199
11:29.103 --> 11:30.696
How about...

200
11:32.111 --> 11:34.111
Let her hold on to you.

201
11:47.774 --> 11:51.365
Ow! Don't pinch her. That hurts!

202
11:55.943 --> 11:57.714
Can you do this one, Pro Vee?

203
12:21.363 --> 12:22.377
Let's just sleep.

204
12:23.848 --> 12:24.895
Oh.

205
12:58.634 --> 13:00.648
I put this here in case you felt uncomfortable.

206
13:01.132 --> 13:03.131
Do I look that uncomfortable?

207
13:03.782 --> 13:08.932
Not really. Just a little awkward.

208
13:09.904 --> 13:10.930
Pro Vee...

209
13:12.057 --> 13:15.676
I'm kidding. You did really well today.

210
13:16.680 --> 13:20.396
- With what? - The brainstorming workshop.

211
13:20.421 --> 13:23.035
I haven't seen everyone that energized in a long time.

212
13:23.187 --> 13:25.864
And I'm going to make all their ideas happen.

213
13:25.889 --> 13:27.398
Just watch me.

214
13:28.134 --> 13:31.401
I will. Now go to sleep.

215
14:32.372 --> 14:34.549
- Good morning. - Good morning.

216
14:34.574 --> 14:37.322
Ooh, new look, new uniforms. So bright and fresh!

217
14:37.347 --> 14:39.306
- Yes. - Oh, and what's this?

218
14:39.331 --> 14:41.513
This is our new air-conditioned golf cart.

219
14:41.538 --> 14:43.985
We're the first course in Thailand to use this model.

220
14:44.010 --> 14:45.431
Wow. Very nice.

221
14:45.456 --> 14:47.298
Which caddie mode would you like today?

222
14:47.323 --> 14:48.337
Serious mode.

223
14:48.362 --> 14:50.209
I've got a tournament at the end of the month.

224
14:50.234 --> 14:52.967
- You got it. Hop in. - Let's go.

225
14:57.626 --> 15:00.084
- Let me turn the AC on for you. - Please do.

226
15:04.392 --> 15:07.769
- Cool enough? - Wow, that's strong. And cold!

227
15:07.808 --> 15:09.779
No waiting for it to cool down either. Very nice.

228
15:09.811 --> 15:11.151
You can adjust the fan speed too.

229
15:11.176 --> 15:13.465
Nice. And the direction.

230
15:13.490 --> 15:15.854
No more hot air blowing from a fan.

231
15:15.879 --> 15:17.688
Excellent.

232
15:24.586 --> 15:26.073
Beautiful shot.

233
15:27.080 --> 15:28.160
Very nice.

234
15:29.233 --> 15:32.907
♪ It's plain to see ♪

235
15:33.410 --> 15:35.071
♪ I know exactly what you think of me ♪

236
15:35.096 --> 15:37.670
♪ First to watch my stories every time ♪

237
15:37.695 --> 15:40.054
Hey, table three is ready to go!

238
15:40.079 --> 15:41.467
Don't keep the customers waiting.

239
15:41.492 --> 15:43.031
Table ten, listen up.

240
15:43.055 --> 15:46.320
The customer is allergic to garlic. No garlic.

241
15:46.345 --> 15:48.923
And this Date on the Green set is really important.

242
15:48.948 --> 15:52.341
When they take photos, I want a million views!

243
15:52.366 --> 15:54.470
- Yes, Chef. - Good.

244
15:54.544 --> 15:55.910
Ready?

245
16:01.223 --> 16:02.608
Give me a heart shape, please.

246
16:03.035 --> 16:05.963
♪ Giving me signs, so why still wait? ♪

247
16:05.988 --> 16:09.434
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

248
16:09.459 --> 16:13.782
♪ How long will you keep playing so tough? ♪

249
16:13.807 --> 16:16.072
Don't force it. Keep your lower body steady.

250
16:21.277 --> 16:22.823
I'm swinging with everything I've got,

251
16:22.848 --> 16:24.111
and the ball barely moves.

252
16:24.135 --> 16:25.692
Focus on a good swing first.

253
16:26.105 --> 16:27.485
Let's try again.

254
16:32.188 --> 16:34.529
Wow, that was beautiful.

255
16:40.737 --> 16:42.229
Okay. Try it.

256
16:44.711 --> 16:48.188
Good. Bring your pinky in.

257
16:48.850 --> 16:52.572
Now swing. Nice! Very good.

258
16:53.003 --> 16:56.917
Great. Now let's look at your backswing.

259
16:57.270 --> 16:59.805
Take it back, shift your weight to the left,

260
16:59.830 --> 17:03.034
make impact, and finish the swing.

261
17:06.291 --> 17:08.644
You actually have a really nice finish.

262
17:13.962 --> 17:15.248
Excellent.

263
17:18.545 --> 17:20.831
This hole looks insanely real.

264
17:20.856 --> 17:23.133
Yeah, playing this makes me want to hit the real course.

265
17:24.527 --> 17:25.765
Sign up for our club today

266
17:25.790 --> 17:27.790
and you'll get a free golf club item in-game.

267
17:27.965 --> 17:30.354
- Then sign me up. - Welcome aboard.

268
17:49.095 --> 17:50.693
What are you smiling about?

269
17:53.023 --> 17:56.016
I'm just happy seeing the course like this.

270
17:56.502 --> 17:58.058
It feels alive again.

271
18:00.227 --> 18:01.284
Tired?

272
18:03.537 --> 18:06.128
Yeah. But I'm not satisfied yet.

273
18:06.153 --> 18:08.306
I think we can take this even further.

274
18:08.901 --> 18:11.538
What else do you think we could do?

275
18:11.948 --> 18:16.272
Maybe we need some fresh inspiration.

276
18:16.297 --> 18:19.037
Something that takes us beyond the usual idea of a golf course.

277
18:33.855 --> 18:35.535
We're going to a fashion show?

278
18:36.060 --> 18:39.275
Oh my God! This is literally my dream.

279
18:39.300 --> 18:41.349
London! Paris! Italy!

280
18:41.374 --> 18:45.359
My chance to finally strut down the runway!

281
18:45.646 --> 18:48.515
Not on the runway, Queen. Next to it.

282
18:48.540 --> 18:50.237
We're watching, not modeling.

283
18:50.572 --> 18:53.251
Don't crush my dreams. Oof!

284
18:53.363 --> 18:54.814
If you weren't the owner's daughter,

285
18:54.839 --> 18:56.451
you'd get another one! Oof!

286
18:57.386 --> 18:59.607
It's my friend's fashion show.

287
18:59.632 --> 19:01.863
But it's not just a regular runway show.

288
19:02.646 --> 19:05.438
Ooh, something wild? Are they going naked?

289
19:05.463 --> 19:08.433
It's a fashion show, Queen. There have to be clothes.

290
19:08.789 --> 19:11.230
And you! Nothing you say is music to my ears either!

291
19:11.255 --> 19:13.780
Honestly, you should be coming to work naked!

292
19:13.805 --> 19:15.474
That's more my style.

293
19:16.109 --> 19:18.125
You'll all find out when we get there.

294
19:18.150 --> 19:21.700
But for this event, I want everyone dressed to the nines.

295
19:23.387 --> 19:26.658
Can I sit this one out? I'm not really into events like that.

296
19:26.683 --> 19:29.652
Nope. We need to get out there and open our minds to new things,

297
19:29.677 --> 19:32.760
not just golf, golf, and more golf.

298
19:32.785 --> 19:34.407
Exactly.

299
19:34.432 --> 19:37.734
And don't worry about your look. I'll take care of everything.

300
19:37.759 --> 19:40.196
Don't forget, I studied fashion.

301
19:40.731 --> 19:43.503
Everyone has to look fabulous. Vas-y!

302
19:43.528 --> 19:46.685
- Huh? Vas-what? - Just say it.

303
19:47.219 --> 19:50.302
- Vas-y! - Vas-y!

304
19:52.456 --> 19:53.717
What the hell does that mean?

305
19:53.742 --> 19:56.036
- Beats the hell outta me. - Huh?

306
20:01.114 --> 20:04.039
I don't think a dress like this would suit me.

307
20:04.064 --> 20:06.430
- Says who? - Me.

308
20:07.519 --> 20:10.347
- Do you ever look in the mirror? - Every day.

309
20:10.547 --> 20:12.906
And you still don't know how beautiful you are?

310
20:12.931 --> 20:14.829
Please try it on for me.

311
20:14.854 --> 20:18.379
It's an evening gown I designed and had made a while ago,

312
20:18.404 --> 20:20.993
but I've never found a model it fit quite right.

313
20:21.018 --> 20:24.306
Please? Just try it on for me.

314
20:25.783 --> 20:28.248
You want me to try it on right here?

315
20:28.273 --> 20:29.860
Yes. I'll help you zip it up.

316
20:29.885 --> 20:31.377
I think I'll change in the bathroom.

317
20:45.044 --> 20:46.125
Are you done yet?

318
20:46.149 --> 20:48.794
I haven't even put it on yet. What's the rush?

319
20:48.819 --> 20:51.073
I just want to see how it looks on you.

320
20:51.098 --> 20:53.876
When I designed this, I revised it so many times.

321
20:53.901 --> 20:56.365
I kept wondering where I'd find the right model for it.

322
20:56.390 --> 20:58.192
But I think it'll look perfect on you.

323
20:58.217 --> 21:00.091
Are you done? Want me to help?

324
21:00.116 --> 21:02.854
It's tricky to put on. Pro Vee!

325
21:04.846 --> 21:06.114
Pro Vee?

326
21:07.902 --> 21:09.830
Are you done yet?

327
21:10.683 --> 21:11.882
Done yet?

328
21:14.154 --> 21:15.614
I want to see.

329
21:16.166 --> 21:19.175
Want me to help? I can help you.

330
21:46.637 --> 21:47.817
So beautiful.

331
21:48.802 --> 21:51.690
The dress or me?

332
21:52.894 --> 21:55.880
A dress doesn't make a woman beautiful.

333
21:55.905 --> 21:58.882
It fills with a beautiful she already has.

334
21:58.907 --> 22:02.500
I still remember that line from my first design class.

335
22:02.525 --> 22:04.324
A dress doesn't make a woman beautiful.

336
22:04.349 --> 22:06.869
It simply reveals the beauty she already has.

337
22:06.894 --> 22:07.943
So, is it beautiful?

338
22:11.096 --> 22:13.280
Come here. I'll zip you up.

339
22:23.642 --> 22:25.462
You have such a beautiful back.

340
22:25.835 --> 22:28.446
You're the first person who's ever complimented my back.

341
22:29.031 --> 22:30.911
For the show, wear your hair up

342
22:30.936 --> 22:32.681
and show off your shoulders and back.

343
22:32.800 --> 22:36.243
Why do I need to show them off to anyone?

344
22:36.727 --> 22:39.539
We don't dress up for other people.

345
22:39.564 --> 22:40.861
Then what for?

346
22:42.035 --> 22:45.544
To show that we're proud of what we have.

347
22:45.569 --> 22:48.381
Why should we hide our own beauty?

348
22:51.114 --> 22:52.291
Look in the mirror.

349
22:57.070 --> 23:00.052
The dress is beautiful. I love it.

350
23:02.479 --> 23:05.019
I should be thanking you.

351
23:05.044 --> 23:07.067
You finally brought this dress back to life

352
23:07.092 --> 23:09.092
after all these years.

353
23:10.699 --> 23:16.314
You've brought a lot of things around here back to life.

354
23:28.802 --> 23:30.642
Pick one. Left or right?

355
23:30.952 --> 23:32.952
Either one. You choose for me.

356
23:33.073 --> 23:34.200
Hmm.

357
23:38.803 --> 23:40.453
This one suits your skin tone.

358
23:40.478 --> 23:42.045
- Take this, Pro Jin. - Okay.

359
23:42.640 --> 23:44.895
I'll go get a garment bag for it.

360
23:47.739 --> 23:50.490
This place is pretty big. How many rooms are there?

361
23:51.903 --> 23:55.859
Two bedrooms, both en suite, and a living room.

362
23:56.560 --> 23:59.353
- You live here alone? - Yes.

363
24:03.634 --> 24:05.100
Have you eaten yet?

364
24:05.512 --> 24:07.369
You mean dinner?

365
24:07.520 --> 24:09.227
- Yeah. - Not yet.

366
24:10.606 --> 24:11.986
Want to grab something to eat?

367
24:24.595 --> 24:27.900
Oh, Mr. Manager! You really are here.

368
24:27.925 --> 24:31.253
Oh, Chef. What can I do for you?

369
24:32.086 --> 24:35.645
Well, I do need something. But just the two of us here...

370
24:35.670 --> 24:38.014
What if people get the wrong idea?

371
24:38.039 --> 24:40.676
- I don't think they will. - I'm kidding.

372
24:40.846 --> 24:43.187
Miss Nana asked me to bring you this outfit.

373
24:43.362 --> 24:46.923
Oh, thanks. Where's yours, Chef Queen?

374
24:47.650 --> 24:50.087
Oh, no. No one can see mine yet.

375
24:50.112 --> 24:52.587
You'll see it at the event. It's a surprise.

376
24:53.930 --> 24:56.166
Chef Queen, take a look at this.

377
24:56.563 --> 24:59.999
Isn't that our former manager?

378
25:02.835 --> 25:07.722
That's March! And that's Ms. Yupadee's course.

379
25:07.926 --> 25:10.940
So he ended up leeching off Ms. Yupadee's course after all.

380
25:12.089 --> 25:14.841
Guys like him always find a way to survive. Impressive.

381
25:19.153 --> 25:22.580
I've approved the project you proposed.

382
25:23.479 --> 25:25.923
Thank you. You can count on me.

383
25:26.253 --> 25:30.723
Do you know who Good View hired to replace you?

384
25:31.636 --> 25:35.262
His name is Nut. He comes from the hotel business.

385
25:35.287 --> 25:36.945
He's never managed a golf course before.

386
25:42.734 --> 25:44.637
I guess they couldn't find anyone better.

387
25:45.415 --> 25:48.552
After all, the one person who knows that place inside and out

388
25:49.890 --> 25:51.626
is already here at The Royal Green.

389
25:55.287 --> 25:59.046
Keep a close eye on everything happening at Good View.

390
26:00.029 --> 26:03.931
I want that course for the lowest possible price.

391
26:05.751 --> 26:06.841
You got it.

392
26:14.908 --> 26:17.712
- Here you go. Rice noodles... - This is the place you picked?

393
26:17.737 --> 26:19.545
- Yep. - Enjoy.

394
26:19.570 --> 26:21.188
Why didn't we go somewhere nicer?

395
26:21.834 --> 26:23.329
What's wrong with this place?

396
26:24.360 --> 26:26.312
It's cheap, simple, quick,

397
26:26.337 --> 26:28.717
convenient, filling, and delicious.

398
26:32.013 --> 26:34.195
- Two chicken noodles, please. - Sure.

399
26:34.220 --> 26:36.255
Dry or with soup today?

400
26:36.805 --> 26:38.567
Pro Jin, dry or with soup?

401
26:38.592 --> 26:40.234
Whatever you're having.

402
26:40.829 --> 26:42.969
And some soup on the side.

403
26:42.994 --> 26:44.994
Sure. Have a seat.

404
26:48.086 --> 26:50.469
You have a way of making everything seem so simple.

405
26:51.288 --> 26:54.647
I just choose whatever makes life less complicated.

406
26:54.854 --> 26:56.544
Do you normally eat at places like this?

407
26:56.729 --> 26:58.717
Sure. Why?

408
26:58.742 --> 27:01.465
You seem more like the expensive-dining type.

409
27:01.893 --> 27:03.605
I can do expensive too.

410
27:03.630 --> 27:05.985
But expensive doesn't always mean delicious.

411
27:06.390 --> 27:10.012
Sometimes simple food like this is much more comforting.

412
27:11.666 --> 27:14.692
You don't look like a golf course CEO's right-hand woman now.

413
27:15.975 --> 27:18.134
Why? What do I look like?

414
27:19.073 --> 27:22.708
Like a third-year student who just finished an assignment

415
27:22.733 --> 27:24.538
and came out for noodles by her dorm.

416
27:25.831 --> 27:28.110
You don't look much like a golf pro either.

417
27:29.252 --> 27:32.464
- What do I look like, then? - Hmm...

418
27:32.807 --> 27:37.084
Like a senior trying to hit on a junior,

419
27:37.109 --> 27:39.840
but he's broke, so he takes her

420
27:39.865 --> 27:41.865
for street-side noodles instead of fine dining.

421
27:43.318 --> 27:49.274
And after dinner, where does this senior take his junior next?

422
27:51.779 --> 27:53.345
Now we're getting a little R-rated.

423
27:58.868 --> 28:03.282
Here we go! Two dry noodles.

424
28:03.307 --> 28:06.375
- And your usual soup. - Thank you.

425
28:07.290 --> 28:09.475
- Enjoy. - Thank you.

426
28:09.500 --> 28:12.080
Want me to pick up some dumplings for you?

427
28:12.105 --> 28:14.533
No, thanks. I can do the picking up myself.

428
28:17.334 --> 28:21.222
Ooh, you've got game! All right, flirt away!

429
28:40.651 --> 28:41.696
Good?

430
29:00.755 --> 29:02.737
- Hey, Nana. - Are you dressed yet?

431
29:02.762 --> 29:05.642
- Dressed for what? - The fashion show I mentioned.

432
29:05.667 --> 29:08.695
That's today? Do I have to go?

433
29:08.720 --> 29:11.832
Five o'clock. We leave on the dot.

434
29:12.583 --> 29:13.651
Yeah, yeah.

435
29:30.967 --> 29:34.085
Thank you. All set. Thank you.

436
30:12.604 --> 30:16.233
- Congratulations! - Thank you. See you inside.

437
30:16.258 --> 30:19.242
Thank you. Oh, Nana!

438
30:20.535 --> 30:27.163
Hello, Fahsai! Fashion's hottest rising star.

439
30:27.479 --> 30:29.773
Thank you for making time for us,

440
30:29.797 --> 30:33.606
Miss Nana of Good View Golf Course.

441
30:33.631 --> 30:37.193
Of course I'm here. Don't forget, fashion is my world.

442
30:37.218 --> 30:42.727
I've just stepped off the runway to run a fairway for a while.

443
30:44.275 --> 30:47.250
This is my team. I brought them here for some inspiration.

444
30:47.275 --> 30:49.457
Maybe we'll find some ideas we can use at the course.

445
30:49.482 --> 30:51.227
Welcome, everyone.

446
30:51.252 --> 30:54.281
It's been ages. You're as beautiful as ever, Fahsai.

447
30:54.546 --> 30:55.768
Thank you, Nut.

448
30:55.792 --> 30:58.967
I heard you're helping Nana run the course now.

449
30:59.174 --> 31:01.138
He's practically the backbone of the place.

450
31:01.582 --> 31:04.720
This is Chef Queen, our head chef.

451
31:04.994 --> 31:06.620
- Hello. - Hello.

452
31:06.645 --> 31:08.527
You look gorgeous tonight.

453
31:08.551 --> 31:11.051
- Just a little something. - Queen!

454
31:11.747 --> 31:14.374
- This is Belle, my assistant. - Hello.

455
31:14.399 --> 31:18.265
This is Pro Jin, Pro Vee, and this is Gus.

456
31:18.290 --> 31:21.015
And our handsome caddies.

457
31:21.999 --> 31:23.626
Make yourselves at home.

458
31:24.408 --> 31:27.840
Hey, all the pros at your course are gorgeous.

459
31:28.070 --> 31:30.725
What a shame. If I'd met them sooner,

460
31:30.750 --> 31:33.223
I'd have put them in tonight's show.

461
31:38.172 --> 31:42.312
But this course does have one hot chef.

462
31:42.337 --> 31:45.404
Think I could model? I've got the look, right?

463
31:45.796 --> 31:47.988
One size fits all, girl. That's the way to go.

464
31:48.013 --> 31:49.742
Werk! Werk!

465
31:49.766 --> 31:54.613
Feel free to do it at my course sometime.

466
31:54.638 --> 31:57.386
- You mean... do the catering? - ใช่

467
31:57.411 --> 32:01.586
Let's stick to catering. Do me and...Bam! Lights out!

468
32:02.945 --> 32:06.518
Okay, everyone, enjoy yourselves. Let's head inside.

469
32:07.109 --> 32:09.959
- We can talk inside. This way. - You look gorgeous.

470
32:09.984 --> 32:13.326
- Girl, the new collection! - You look amazing tonight.

471
33:58.750 --> 34:01.735
- Beautiful. - Gorgeous.

472
34:27.764 --> 34:29.227
It's beautiful, isn't it, Pro Vee?

473
34:29.973 --> 34:32.403
Yeah. It's interesting.

474
34:32.428 --> 34:36.874
Normally, cars and fashion are presented separately.

475
34:36.899 --> 34:39.052
Each has its own story.

476
34:39.189 --> 34:42.618
People may lose interest because it's nothing new.

477
34:42.880 --> 34:45.670
But put them together, and you create something new.

478
34:46.877 --> 34:51.232
What's even more interesting is how it attracts new audiences.

479
34:51.653 --> 34:55.503
Both car enthusiasts and people interested in fashion.

480
34:57.814 --> 34:59.295
What are you thinking, Nana?

481
35:00.002 --> 35:03.155
If a vintage garage can become a runway,

482
35:03.180 --> 35:04.776
what about our fairway?

483
35:07.700 --> 35:08.900
What could it become?

484
35:12.210 --> 35:14.842
I'm gonna go to the restroom real quick.

485
35:33.746 --> 35:35.955
Oh, Fahsai.

486
35:38.116 --> 35:42.961
Pro Vee, perfect timing. I could use a little help.

487
35:42.986 --> 35:43.998
Yes?

488
35:44.022 --> 35:48.103
My zipper's stuck. I can't get it to budge.

489
35:48.128 --> 35:50.128
Could you help me?

490
35:50.955 --> 35:52.011
Sure.

491
36:04.301 --> 36:10.044
Thank you. I'd better get back to my guests. See you inside.

492
36:10.674 --> 36:12.462
- Sure. - Thank you.

493
36:27.408 --> 36:30.584
Fahsai, tonight's show was amazing.

494
36:30.609 --> 36:33.945
I loved how you paired the fashion with the cars.

495
36:33.970 --> 36:36.846
Thanks. I'm glad you liked it.

496
36:36.871 --> 36:38.735
I've always trusted your taste.

497
36:38.877 --> 36:42.428
- You just gave me an idea. - An idea? What kind?

498
36:43.241 --> 36:45.418
I'm putting on a fashion show at the golf course.

499
36:46.688 --> 36:48.735
I'm turning the fairway into a runway.

500
36:48.760 --> 36:51.180
Ooh, interesting. I like it.

501
36:51.205 --> 36:53.736
That'll be the longest runway I've ever seen.

502
36:53.785 --> 36:56.996
It'll take the models all day just to walk the whole thing.

503
36:57.337 --> 36:59.585
I'm not kidding. I'm serious.

504
36:59.610 --> 37:02.413
- Be my consultant. - Sure. No problem.

505
37:08.975 --> 37:10.873
Did you enjoy the show, Pro Vee?

506
37:11.547 --> 37:14.224
- It was beautiful. - Thank you.

507
37:19.682 --> 37:22.885
We should probably get going now.

508
37:22.910 --> 37:27.215
Don't forget about the golf course runway. I'm serious.

509
37:28.646 --> 37:31.298
I won't. I'll come by the course.

510
37:32.684 --> 37:35.653
You'd better! I'm waiting to show off my skills.

511
37:35.916 --> 37:39.249
- I will. - I'll be ready to welcome you.

512
37:39.658 --> 37:42.991
All right. See you soon.

513
37:58.372 --> 38:00.926
You've insisted on driving me home twice now.

514
38:01.187 --> 38:04.768
Should I take that as a sign, Pro Jin?

515
38:07.370 --> 38:10.427
I'll pay you for both rides today and last time.

516
38:10.657 --> 38:13.421
- It's fine. - How is it fine?

517
38:13.769 --> 38:15.568
You said you'd charge me interest too.

518
38:16.380 --> 38:18.643
Consider it payment for finding me an outfit today.

519
38:18.917 --> 38:22.006
Miss Nana found the outfit, not me.

520
38:22.363 --> 38:24.173
Let me transfer you the fare.

521
38:24.198 --> 38:26.670
I feel bad making you drive me home twice.

522
38:26.695 --> 38:29.957
Don't overthink it. We're coworkers.

523
38:29.982 --> 38:32.254
Coworkers. Not friends.

524
38:34.502 --> 38:35.763
Want to be friends?

525
38:36.875 --> 38:38.146
So you're not flirting with me.

526
38:52.837 --> 38:53.925
Wait.

527
38:58.999 --> 39:00.004
What was that?

528
39:02.181 --> 39:03.292
Nothing.

529
39:03.662 --> 39:06.575
Why do you suddenly want to be friends with me?

530
39:07.979 --> 39:09.476
Why can't we be?

531
39:10.397 --> 39:12.405
Is there a limit on how many friends you can have?

532
39:13.486 --> 39:14.836
Well... no.

533
39:15.896 --> 39:17.388
Then that's a yes.

534
39:19.126 --> 39:20.205
Fine.

535
39:21.271 --> 39:24.839
Then thanks for driving me home twice.

536
39:26.183 --> 39:27.992
I'll drive you home as many times as you want.

537
39:31.866 --> 39:33.358
When do I have to return this dress?

538
39:33.383 --> 39:34.421
As soon as possible.

539
39:34.446 --> 39:35.785
Want me to take it off right here?

540
39:35.810 --> 39:38.557
Hey! No. Tomorrow's fine.

541
39:45.134 --> 39:46.202
Good night.

542
40:14.030 --> 40:17.584
Abigail, get those ready. Oh, that's wrapped beautifully.

543
40:17.609 --> 40:20.865
Just not quite fast enough. Come on, customers are coming!

544
40:22.566 --> 40:23.679
Nana!

545
40:23.704 --> 40:25.695
- Fahsai! - Hi.

546
40:25.720 --> 40:27.213
You didn't tell me you were coming.

547
40:27.238 --> 40:29.737
I had some business nearby, so I thought I'd stop by.

548
40:29.762 --> 40:32.917
And we can talk about that fashion show idea of yours.

549
40:32.942 --> 40:36.277
Oh, you're putting on a fashion show at the golf course?

550
40:36.302 --> 40:38.822
It's just an idea for now, Queen.

551
40:38.847 --> 40:41.045
Is Pro Vee here today?

552
40:42.308 --> 40:44.198
Oh! Perfect timing.

553
40:44.490 --> 40:47.568
Hi, Fahsai. Here for a round?

554
40:47.624 --> 40:49.145
I'm here to look around.

555
40:49.170 --> 40:52.008
Nana wants to put on a fashion show here.

556
40:52.972 --> 40:56.814
Looks like I'll need you to show me around today.

557
40:59.059 --> 41:01.129
Pro Vee probably has lessons.

558
41:03.155 --> 41:06.428
I'm free right now. My next lesson isn't until this evening.

559
41:07.927 --> 41:09.133
Perfect.

560
41:09.158 --> 41:12.900
Perfect for you too, Miss Nana. You're free right now.

561
41:12.925 --> 41:14.877
Go with your best friend.

562
41:14.902 --> 41:18.791
You still have urgent documents to review, Miss Nana.

563
41:18.816 --> 41:20.283
They're not finished yet.

564
41:26.339 --> 41:28.434
Nana, you don't have to come.

565
41:28.458 --> 41:31.455
Pro Vee and I can go by ourselves.

566
41:33.249 --> 41:35.114
- Shall we? - Sure.

567
41:35.519 --> 41:36.542
Okay.

568
41:46.475 --> 41:50.674
Looks like your best friend is about to steal your girl.

569
41:57.531 --> 42:00.701
This golf course is actually really beautiful.

570
42:01.507 --> 42:05.224
The green grass against the blue sky,

571
42:05.249 --> 42:08.074
the hills, the water...

572
42:10.098 --> 42:12.342
Do you play golf, Fahsai?

573
42:12.770 --> 42:16.138
I don't really exercise at all. It's exhausting.

574
42:16.163 --> 42:19.547
It's hot, you get all sticky... not my idea of fun.

575
42:20.079 --> 42:23.766
Give golf a try. I promise you'll fall for it.

576
42:24.067 --> 42:25.331
Now that sounds interesting.

577
42:25.996 --> 42:28.420
I wouldn't mind falling.

578
42:29.967 --> 42:33.886
Then once you get the hang of it, you should come play a round.

579
42:34.130 --> 42:38.287
If you're just starting out, you could begin with nine holes

580
42:38.312 --> 42:41.220
and finish over there. See?

581
42:41.561 --> 42:43.875
What are those two whispering about over there?

582
42:45.487 --> 42:47.010
What are you staring at, Miss Nana?

583
42:48.727 --> 42:49.759
Nothing.

584
42:49.999 --> 42:53.818
Maybe you should take a look at your own heart instead.

585
42:53.843 --> 42:57.406
It's running hotter than this fairway right now.

586
43:00.155 --> 43:01.200
Queen!

587
43:02.731 --> 43:05.973
Are you jealous over your friend or over your pro?

588
43:06.309 --> 43:09.395
Don't answer. I already know.

589
43:12.046 --> 43:16.268
Would an area like that be available for us to use?

590
43:16.375 --> 43:17.667
It does look beautiful.

591
43:17.692 --> 43:21.441
We may need to ask your friend who owns the course.

592
43:21.590 --> 43:25.524
- Ooh, are they about to hug? - Queen!

593
43:26.090 --> 43:29.393
Maybe even kiss... Ow!

594
43:46.334 --> 43:47.971
Where's Eve? We had a lesson scheduled.

595
43:47.996 --> 43:51.170
She said she doesn't like waiting, so she already left.

596
43:51.195 --> 43:54.125
Why were you late today? She was a new client too.

597
43:54.150 --> 43:57.017
They closed a road, so traffic was backed up.

598
44:03.646 --> 44:06.180
Oh, Pro Jin. What's up?

599
44:06.363 --> 44:08.928
I wanted to apologize.

600
44:09.358 --> 44:10.907
For being late today?

601
44:11.082 --> 44:13.796
Yes. We ended up losing a client because of me.

602
44:13.982 --> 44:15.831
I already called her.

603
44:15.855 --> 44:17.914
I threw in an extra hour, and she calmed down.

604
44:18.818 --> 44:20.271
Just don't be late again.

605
44:22.947 --> 44:26.326
I wanted to ask about the staff housing.

606
44:26.926 --> 44:30.578
Would it be possible for me to stay here too?

607
44:30.603 --> 44:32.453
My place is pretty far away,

608
44:32.682 --> 44:35.790
and if housing is provided for the golf pros here,

609
44:35.815 --> 44:38.377
I figured I might be eligible too.

610
44:39.299 --> 44:43.219
Well, it's not exactly an official benefit.

611
44:43.664 --> 44:45.902
We just try to help where we can.

612
44:46.734 --> 44:50.241
But I think all the houses are occupied now. Right, Belle?

613
44:50.681 --> 44:53.584
Mm. Yes.

614
44:54.841 --> 44:56.547
The houses are full,

615
44:56.571 --> 44:59.368
but I think there's still a spare bedroom.

616
45:01.203 --> 45:02.299
What do you mean?

617
45:03.217 --> 45:05.906
There's a two-bedroom house

618
45:05.931 --> 45:08.272
with only one person living in it.

619
45:41.785 --> 45:45.361
So, Aom, give us an update. How's married life?

620
45:45.829 --> 45:47.775
Still fabulous.

621
45:47.800 --> 45:49.378
You girls should try marriage sometime.

622
45:49.403 --> 45:51.558
- Let's hope it stays fabulous.

623
45:52.103 --> 45:55.095
Fahsai, look at that dreamy little smile.

624
45:55.120 --> 45:56.465
There's definitely someone.

625
45:56.489 --> 46:01.426
Exactly. Normally, our Fahsai never shuts up.

626
46:01.451 --> 46:06.107
Come on, tell us. Who's the poor guy?

627
46:06.976 --> 46:13.156
We met at my runway show, and again just now.

628
46:13.181 --> 46:15.340
What? Who?

629
46:15.365 --> 46:17.469
Then we must've met too.

630
46:17.494 --> 46:19.494
Exactly. Who is it, Fahsai?

631
46:21.355 --> 46:23.870
A pro golfer.

632
46:26.729 --> 46:32.278
Ooh, so you're leaving the runway for the fairway now, bestie?

633
46:32.839 --> 46:35.414
Oh, stop it. Just eat. What did you order?

634
46:35.439 --> 46:37.232
- Come on, tell us everything. - No.

635
46:37.257 --> 46:39.935
- So? How's the swing? - Spill!

636
46:39.960 --> 46:42.735
I said we met at a fashion show. What swing?

637
46:42.760 --> 46:44.339
Are you sure? Be honest.

638
46:44.363 --> 46:46.129
Just eat. Why are you so obsessed with me?

639
46:46.154 --> 46:49.396
- Have some cake first. - Tell us! We want to know.

640
46:49.421 --> 46:52.934
- Come on, tell us! - Right now!

641
46:59.395 --> 47:01.466
Am I making you uncomfortable

642
47:01.491 --> 47:04.006
or invading your privacy by moving in?

643
47:04.438 --> 47:07.806
- Don't overthink it. - Then, thank you.

644
47:09.238 --> 47:11.109
But I do have some house rules.

645
47:11.593 --> 47:12.799
Let's hear them.

646
47:12.824 --> 47:15.021
One, no practicing golf indoors.

647
47:15.172 --> 47:17.955
Two, don't leave the lights on all night.

648
47:18.026 --> 47:20.245
Three, no overnight guests.

649
47:20.270 --> 47:23.637
- Are these course rules or... - My rules.

650
47:25.258 --> 47:27.659
Deal. You were here first.

651
47:28.222 --> 47:29.486
Thank you.

652
47:29.511 --> 47:31.599
- But the same goes for you. - What does?

653
47:31.624 --> 47:33.172
No overnight guests.

654
47:33.436 --> 47:35.007
I don't have anyone anyway.

655
47:35.698 --> 47:37.380
- You're single? - Mm-hmm.

656
47:38.190 --> 47:40.232
So am I.

657
47:53.531 --> 47:59.561
Food's here, Miss Nana! And it looks amazing.

658
48:00.732 --> 48:04.170
Aren't you busy, Chef? Why are you serving it yourself?

659
48:04.273 --> 48:07.107
Oh, the kitchen is absolutely slammed today.

660
48:07.132 --> 48:08.806
We can barely keep up.

661
48:09.507 --> 48:12.179
Let the others take a break. I can handle this.

662
48:12.888 --> 48:15.133
But Miss Nana, what are you doing up here?

663
48:15.158 --> 48:18.701
So much work you can't even eat at the clubhouse?

664
48:18.726 --> 48:21.990
I'm working on some plans. I got a little carried away.

665
48:22.746 --> 48:26.151
Don't spend all your time working.

666
48:26.429 --> 48:28.718
You might regret it later.

667
48:29.021 --> 48:30.411
What do you mean?

668
48:30.618 --> 48:33.597
Someone you know very well

669
48:33.622 --> 48:36.240
just signed up for golf lessons.

670
48:37.412 --> 48:41.118
And right now, they're enjoying each other...oops,

671
48:42.303 --> 48:45.282
I mean, enjoying a meal at the clubhouse.

672
48:45.713 --> 48:46.864
Who?

673
48:49.420 --> 48:51.807
Clear Sky.

674
48:53.069 --> 48:54.889
Clear... Sky?

675
48:54.914 --> 48:57.684
Clear. Sky.

676
48:59.859 --> 49:01.128
Fahsai!

677
49:03.411 --> 49:04.805
Eating alone?

678
49:12.848 --> 49:17.118
Careful, don't knock that over. I made it especially for you.

679
49:17.143 --> 49:18.298
I won't.

680
49:34.173 --> 49:35.958
I'm not sure either.

681
49:36.301 --> 49:39.420
- Would you like some shrimp? - Thank you.

682
49:47.250 --> 49:50.361
- Feeling possessive? - Jealous.

683
49:55.234 --> 49:57.361
Queen, you put laxatives in that, right?

684
49:57.687 --> 49:59.571
Oh! I could never do that!

685
49:59.596 --> 50:01.994
That violates the global chef code of ethics!

686
50:04.015 --> 50:06.675
But how about this?

687
50:06.700 --> 50:09.484
I'll have someone carry over a bright-colored drink,

688
50:09.509 --> 50:13.209
Then... Oops! Spill it all over them.

689
50:13.234 --> 50:15.051
That way, they'll have to split up.

690
50:15.076 --> 50:17.076
Good idea, right?

691
50:18.816 --> 50:21.773
I'm not the villain here, Queen.

692
50:25.647 --> 50:27.263
I'm the heroine.

693
50:30.202 --> 50:33.705
"Pro Vee, try this. It's really good."

694
50:33.730 --> 50:36.985
"Sure. It must be delicious."

695
50:37.197 --> 50:39.260
Give it a minute. They'll be all over each other.

696
50:43.643 --> 50:49.291
Calm down. Calm down, girl. Calm down.

697
50:50.751 --> 50:52.132
Hold it like this.

698
50:53.060 --> 50:55.664
That's right. and put your right hand over it.

699
50:56.707 --> 50:59.532
Even holding the club properly is hard.

700
51:02.332 --> 51:05.523
Pro Vee, you hold golf clubs every day.

701
51:05.548 --> 51:08.137
How are your hands still so soft?

702
51:23.357 --> 51:26.342
Carry over a bright-colored drink, serve it to them,

703
51:26.367 --> 51:28.794
and spill the whole thing.

704
51:28.819 --> 51:30.654
That way, they'll have to split up.

705
51:30.813 --> 51:33.059
I'm not the villain here, Queen.

706
51:34.050 --> 51:35.638
I'm the heroine.

707
51:35.663 --> 51:38.893
She went in with a vengeance,

708
51:38.918 --> 51:42.198
determined to complete her mission.

709
51:48.416 --> 51:52.127
Whoosh! Villain-in-training.

710
51:54.304 --> 51:56.460
Nana, what are you doing over there?

711
51:56.936 --> 51:58.256
Are you okay?

712
51:59.182 --> 52:01.871
- I'm fine. I'm fine. - You're soaked.

713
52:02.805 --> 52:07.215
I was going to bring you some water, but I spilled it all.

714
52:11.999 --> 52:13.098
Did you hurt yourself?

715
52:14.559 --> 52:17.376
I'm fine. It's nothing.

716
52:19.871 --> 52:23.294
Guess your revenge wasn't strong enough, Miss Nana.

717
52:38.329 --> 52:42.092
Are you tired? You've been awfully quiet since Fahsai left.

718
52:42.623 --> 52:43.642
No.

719
52:44.963 --> 52:48.154
Pro Vee, can I ask you something straight?

720
52:48.709 --> 52:49.719
Sure.

721
52:51.841 --> 52:53.630
What do you think of Fahsai?

722
52:53.836 --> 52:56.036
What do you mean?

723
52:56.489 --> 53:01.288
You've only met her a few times,

724
53:01.313 --> 53:03.137
but you two already seem pretty close.

725
53:03.483 --> 53:04.569
Jealous?

726
53:11.777 --> 53:13.331
Yes, Fahsai?

727
53:15.796 --> 53:18.432
My schedule's packed right now.

728
53:18.457 --> 53:21.583
I'll have the course book you in for another day.

729
53:21.925 --> 53:24.535
Sorry about that. Okay.

730
53:26.590 --> 53:28.084
You have her number too?

731
53:28.843 --> 53:30.803
I don't even have yours.

732
53:31.120 --> 53:32.377
Give me your phone.

733
53:48.324 --> 53:51.492
So... do you have feelings for Fahsai?

734
53:51.904 --> 53:53.278
What kind of feelings?

735
53:55.150 --> 53:57.053
Do you like her?

736
54:00.527 --> 54:04.894
Why do you ask? Are you jealous or possessive?

737
54:04.919 --> 54:06.426
Am I allowed to be?

738
54:07.948 --> 54:09.107
Allowed to be what?

739
54:11.068 --> 54:13.952
Am I allowed to be jealous over you?

740
54:15.515 --> 54:19.011
Good question. Do you want to be?

741
54:22.126 --> 54:25.805
If you do, you'd better start staking your claim.

742
54:27.027 --> 54:31.328
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

743
54:32.143 --> 54:36.063
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

744
54:36.088 --> 54:38.088
(Nana's Vee)

745
54:38.113 --> 54:41.840
♪ Together, we'll race toward the line ♪

746
54:43.640 --> 54:46.190
Hello, my Nana.

747
54:47.437 --> 54:52.630
♪ In the end, I know we'll make it there ♪

748
54:52.655 --> 54:56.975
♪ Just one rule for you and me to share ♪

749
54:57.485 --> 55:00.798
♪ Promise you'll stay close to me ♪

750
55:00.823 --> 55:03.349
♪ Hold me in your arms so tenderly ♪

751
55:03.374 --> 55:06.878
♪ I've never bowed to anyone in sight ♪

752
55:06.903 --> 55:11.663
I wonder if there's room here for your Nana too.

753
55:11.982 --> 55:13.982
Have you seen the news about Goodview's event?

754
55:14.776 --> 55:18.162
The fashion show thing?

755
55:18.435 --> 55:21.364
It's a golf course. It's right there in the name.

756
55:21.389 --> 55:23.453
Nana must've completely lost it.

757
55:23.478 --> 55:28.210
What if that six-year-old girl still stands by her promise

758
55:29.173 --> 55:34.383
and has come back to claim it? What would you say, Pro Vee?

759
55:38.476 --> 55:42.691
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

760
55:43.448 --> 55:48.555
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

761
55:48.580 --> 55:53.209
♪ Together, we'll race toward the line ♪

762
55:53.776 --> 55:58.270
♪ Chasing the dream that's yours and mine ♪

763
55:58.815 --> 56:03.953
♪ In the end, I know we'll make it there ♪

764
56:03.978 --> 56:08.260
♪ Just one rule for you and me to share ♪

765
56:09.070 --> 56:12.215
♪ Promise you'll stay close to me ♪

766
56:12.240 --> 56:14.695
♪ Hold me in your arms so tenderly ♪

767
56:14.720 --> 56:20.254
♪ I've never bowed to anyone in sight ♪

768
56:20.279 --> 56:23.346
♪ But for you, I'd surrender without a fight ♪

769
56:23.371 --> 56:27.611
♪ Just take my hand and hold it tight ♪

770
56:29.488 --> 56:32.635
♪ And walk with me along the way ♪

771
56:32.660 --> 56:35.209
♪ No matter what it takes to win someday ♪

772
56:35.234 --> 56:40.528
♪ Sometimes this tender heart may despair ♪

773
56:41.002 --> 56:44.195
♪ But tell me, why should we care? ♪

774
56:44.220 --> 56:46.548
♪ When all we need is love that's fair ♪

775
56:46.573 --> 56:50.217
♪ In a love we share, no one has to win or lose ♪

776
56:52.452 --> 56:56.985
♪ Let my heart answer anew ♪

777
56:57.602 --> 57:02.124
♪ A thousand rounds, it'd still choose you ♪

778
57:02.689 --> 57:07.247
♪ One look in your eyes is all I need ♪

779
57:07.560 --> 57:11.267
♪ Oh, baby. I trust your sweet. ♪
